Z||000005||TheFiero64||01-03-2001||04:33 PM||||I will never deal with them again unless they learn to speed up a lot. I have called them every name in the book wile I waited for my parts. With the Fiero Store I get everything the very next day.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cooter||01-03-2001||06:34 PM||||When I was getting ready to put the 3.4 in my car, I ordered a truck load of stuff from them- like a clutch kit, clutch master/slaves for 3 Fieros, shocks/struts, plugs and wire. It took over 2 months for the stuff to start coming in. Every part came from a different location and in a seperate box (One was a pilot shaft bushing in a small box by itself!) Of everything I ordered, only one clutch slave was right- some of the parts were just crap- it looked like returned items that someone else could get to work. The clutch had greasy hand prints all over it, the "new" master/slave cylinders were pouring brake fluid out in the greasy boxes and some of the parts just never came in. I finally got tired of waiting and sent all the stuff back with a nasty letter of my displeasure with their parts and service. I will NEVER order from them again.||||reg||1
