Z||000008||Seanh||01-03-2001||10:24 PM||||I had tons of trouble with Carparts.com last summer. I ordered a 4" lift kit for my '85 Bronco and they took around 6 weeks to get it here. And then to top it off, they sent me the 3" lift, not the 4" lift I ordered, but I just took it and they refunded the difference and I was ok with it I guess. I will not order from them again, but they did take offer to take care of the mix-up or refund the difference if I just keep the one I got. I would definatly say to order from Fiero Store.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I><p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 01-03-2001).]||||reg||1
